  "answer": "Based on my research, the Pokémon is **Incineroar**. Here's the complete comparison:\n\n## Summary\n- **WolfeyVGC's hated mainstay**: Incineroar — he ranks it his \"fourth most hated Pokémon\" (\"incredibly poorly designed\" for game balance) but admits it's \"the best supporting Pokémon we've ever had\" and uses it on championship teams (2024 Worlds, 2025 EUIC winner, official Mystery Gift distribution) [1]\n- **Pachirisu's first Worlds win**: 2014 (VGC 2014, Gen 6, Pokémon X & Y) — Se-Jun Park won Masters Division [2]\n- **Incineroar's first Worlds win**: 2018 (VGC 2018, Gen 7, Pokémon Sun/Moon) — Paul Ruiz won Masters Division [3]\n\n## Base Stats Comparison\n\n| Stat | **Incineroar** (Gen 7, 2018 Worlds debut) | **Pachirisu** (Gen 6, 2014 Worlds debut) |\n|------|--------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|\n| HP | 95 | 60 |\n| Attack | 115 | 45 |\n| Defense | 90 | 70 |\n| Special Attack | 80 | 45 |\n| Special Defense | 90 | 90 |\n| Speed | 60 | 95 |\n| **Total** | **530** | **405** |\n\n[4][5]\n\n## Key Differences\n- **Incineroar** has **+125 BST advantage** (530 vs 405)\n- Incineroar dominates physically: **+70 Attack, +20 Defense, +35 SpA, +35 HP**\n- Pachirisu is faster: **+35 Speed** (95 vs 60)\n- Both share **90 SpD**, but Incineroar's higher HP gives it better overall special bulk\n- Incineroar's Fire/Dark typing + Intimidate + Fake Out/Parting Shot/Knock Off movepool made it competitively mandatory despite Wolfey's hatred\n\n## Sources\n1. https://www.yahoo.com/entertainment/articles/pokemon-prophecy-come-pass-former-162251221.html\n2. https://www.pokemon.com/us/play-pokemon/worlds/2014/teams/masters\n3. https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/World_Championships\n4. https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Incineroar_(Pok%C3%A9mon)\n5. https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Pachirisu_(Pok%C3%A9mon)",
